**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`

**How to implement.** The acceptance facts (step 481) run one noisy fit of each existing design, so the noisy-experiment runners leave their classes for the shared test support (the S14.1 mapper's note: '`perturbedStart`, `scalingAround` and the noisy-ensemble helpers are still MuellerInverseTests class bindings, to move if a layer-2 fact needs them'; 001 §Q 'The ground truth and designs … move into a shared test-support project'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Each is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … a move'): one declaration of each moved name exists afterwards, and BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'). `BerremanTestSupport` references no test framework (step 344), so a moved runner answers the product's `Result` and its callers pipe it through `expectOk` (step 335). Each moved doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines, citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/QuartzSample.fs` (step 473), after `fullConfigurations`, opening the product modules where the compiler asks: `solverParameters` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:solverParameters`, three reflections, its reason kept in one line); `forward` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:forward`, `createBerremanForward` of the uniaxial builder as S10.1 leaves it, `fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties`, step 332); `quartzScalingAround` (the class's `scalingAround`, `MuellerInverseTests.fs:scalingAround`, renamed as `AbsorbingBiaxialSample` names its own `absorbingScalingAround`, so no reader's `open` shadows `MuellerFitting.scalingAround`, step 336); `blindStart` and `wideBox` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:blindStart`, `:wideBox`); `noisyQuartzObservations (noise : NoiseParam) (seed : NoiseSeed) (configurations : MeasurementConfiguration list) : Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`, the class's `noisyObserve` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:noisyObserve`) without its `expectOk`: `noisyObserveWith forward quartz noise seed configurations` (step 339); and `recoverQuartzFromNoisy (noise : NoiseParam) (seed : NoiseSeed) : Result<NoisyExperiment<UniaxialParameters>, MuellerFitError>`, the class's `recoverFromNoisy` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:recoverFromNoisy`): `noisyQuartzObservations noise seed fullConfigurations`, then `MuellerFitting.fitObservations forward wideBox <them> (quartzScalingAround blindStart)` (step 337), then `{ seed = seed; fit = <its MuellerFitData> }` (step 341). The record `fitWithResidual` answers holds the scaling, residual and solution the class's literal rebuilt it from, `recovered` being `ofScaled scaling solution.solution` in both (step 337), so every number is unchanged. `MuellerInverseTests.fs` deletes the seven and reads them from `QuartzSample` as it reads the moved design (step 473); its `noisyObserve` uses become `noisyQuartzObservations … |> expectOk` and its `recoverFromNoisy` uses `recoverQuartzFromNoisy … |> expectOk`; its own `fitObservations` wrapper, `runFit`, `observe`, `perturbedStart`, `nearBox` and `recoveredQuantities` stay, over the moved `forward` and `quartzScalingAround`. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (steps 346, 431), after `absorbingBandBreaches`: `absorbingForward`, the class's `forward` (`AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs:forward`: `createBerremanForward` of the absorbing builder over `BiaxialSample.solverParameters`, step 334), and `recoverAbsorbingFromNoisy (noise : NoiseParam) (seed : NoiseSeed) : Result<NoisyExperiment<AbsorbingTriclinicParameters>, MuellerFitError>`, the class's `recoverFromNoisy` (`AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs:recoverFromNoisy`): `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith absorbingForward absorbing noise seed fullConfigurations` (step 340), then `fitAbsorbingObservations absorbingForward searchBox <them> (absorbingScalingAround perturbedStart)` (step 337), then the record. `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` deletes its `forward` and `recoverFromNoisy` and maps `noisySeeds` (step 431) through `recoverAbsorbingFromNoisy NoiseParam.decentLab … |> expectOk`. `KitAcceptanceTests`' own observation helper (step 434) is not touched. No test is added or removed.

**Acceptance.** After the moves, `QuartzSample` MUST declare `solverParameters`, `forward`, `quartzScalingAround`, `blindStart`, `wideBox`, `noisyQuartzObservations` and `recoverQuartzFromNoisy`, and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample` `absorbingForward` and `recoverAbsorbingFromNoisy`, each once and answering `Result`, with `MuellerInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` reading them and declaring none; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` and `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
